              Facts are his (articles, ABOUT-ME, and what he said on 10/9). Still Claude's reading, unconfirmed: 「什麼時候該求快、什麼時候一步都不能省，我分得出來」.
              Not re-checked: 每月超過 15 萬次閱讀／三個月內／四個月做了 AI Resume Advisor／5 月上線時是第一批使用者. */}
          <p>我在科技業待了二十年，Nokia、聯詠科技、友達光電：七年工程師、十年 PM、三年數據分析與事業單位主管（BU Head）的幕僚。PM 那十年，我管過時程很趕的手機，也負責過時程長、開發嚴謹的車用電子，那是兩個很不一樣的生態。產品規劃、商業決策、跨部門協調，該會的都碰過，遇到什麼事大概知道下一步該怎麼走。</p>
          <p>但做越久越覺得在原地踏步。能力在長，可是每天的精力都花在讓別人同意我做事上面。</p>
          <p>2019 年，公司把整個手機部門搬去中國，我選擇不去，十年累積的人脈和成就幾乎歸零。隔年我開始寫日記，第一天寫下的問題是：「明知當前生活並非理想，如何鼓起勇氣脫離舒適圈？」</p>
          <p class="pull">2023 年，我決定回去當學生。</p>
          <p>我去唸 Minerva University 的碩士，重新學怎麼做決策。2025 年，我離開公司，剛好 Claude Code 在那年 5 月上線。我是第一批使用者，開始用它做產品：四個月做了 <a href="https://airesumeadvisor.com/zh-TW/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI Resume Advisor</a>，三天做了 <a href="https://www.neatoolkit.com/zh-TW" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NeatToolkit</a>。</p>
          <p>一開始我只拿它做產品，從概念、開發到上線推廣，每一段都自己走過。後來目標、每天的工作、學到的東西、客戶、生活，一塊一塊都搬了上去。</p>
          {/* 10/9: this was one eight-line paragraph — "還是很長，沒有呼吸感". Now a lead sentence and three short "before / now" pairs,
              set a little closer together so they read as one group. Third pair, the author's correction: say 事業單位主管的幕僚 (not 經營管理部門), and the work was strategy recommendations backed by data. Then corrected again: the order is data → insight → strategy; 「提策略建議，並且拿數據支撐它」 read as strategy first, data found afterwards. The 'now' half was then lifted from the weekly score ("層次太低") to the same level as the 'before' half: numbers first, then where to put his effort. Then lifted once more: the three named numbers (articles read, sign-ups, where time goes) are real but "太具體" — the 'now' half now sits at the same level as the 'before' half. Shortened on the way: 「第一件事」 and the unconfirmed
              「以前跟工程師約好什麼叫做完」 are gone. */}
          <p>做這些事的方法，是過去二十年練出來的。</p>
          <p class="ex">以前開專案，要先寫 Project Charter，一份講清楚為什麼做、要做到哪裡的文件。現在不管是一個產品還是這一季的目標，我一樣先把它寫清楚。</p>
          <p class="ex">定義問題、拆解需求、驗收產出，是 PM 每天在做的事。以前對象是工程師，現在是 AI。</p>
          <p class="ex">以前當事業單位主管的幕僚，我的工作是從數據裡找出洞見，再形成策略建議。現在對自己的事業也是這樣，先從數據裡看出發生了什麼，再決定往哪裡走。</p>
          <p class="ex">以前在公司裡，我主導過 Jira、Polarion 的導入，也訂過專案管理、問題解決和變更的流程，知道理想和實務的落差會出現在哪裡。現在帶團隊把 AI 接進流程，用的是同一份經驗。</p>
          {/* 10/9, the author's correction. Claude had written 「這二十年教會我怎麼把事情做出來，卻沒有教我先想清楚要去哪裡」 to join two paragraphs —
              wrong, and invented. His account: a PM starts from a Project Charter, which IS the direction; so his system starts from goals too;
              these are methods he already had, and they sit naturally in a working environment shared with AI.
              Also his: gloss "Project Charter" in plain words; 「我的系統也是從這些方法來的」 was too crude.
              The last clause (AI takes the doing; direction and acceptance stay with him) is from his article agentic-coding-guide.
              The tool-chasing paragraph went back to 「我相信的事」. The unconfirmed phones/automotive "so I can tell…" sentence is gone. */}
          {/* 10/9 again: the separate paragraph about "my work system" is removed at the author's word ("不要去講另外一套工作系統…
              用例子來補充，讓上面這一段變得更豐滿"). The point is only: what he did before, he now does with AI. So the paragraph above carries
              one example per habit — the charter (his, 10/9), agreeing what "done" means (article loop-engineering), the weekly numbers (personal-panopticon).
              10/9 later: the scope was too narrow (read as "a man who builds products with AI"). The product is where it started; goals, daily work,
              what he learns, clients and life followed — his own list (article flux-direction-system-leverage). The author confirmed this reading.
              10/9 later: 「看數字下判斷」 did not say which numbers or which judgement. Now: before = testing which strategy has better odds
              (his article 數據分析師); now = the weekly score, how much of the week's commitments got done, and what he decides from it
              (articles 12-week-year-guide, personal-panopticon). Other numbers he may want here instead (traffic, sign-ups) — asked, not yet answered.
              Removed text: 我現在每天用的那套工作系統，骨架是 PM 的方法。PM 做專案，一開始要寫 Project Charter…方向和驗收還是照原來的方法走。 */}
          <p class="pull">我把這些過程寫下來。</p>
          {/* 10/9: everything from here to the end of the story rewritten after talking it through with the author. He read the old version as
              contrived — written to sell. His account: AI and productivity are what he is interested in anyway; he is glad to share the road and the
              pitfalls (the articles ARE the sharing); he built his own products first, but what people asked about was his AI working environment,
              his workflow and how he uses AI; that sharing later became income of its own accord; interest + helping people + income is the life
              he wants — the direction is right, he is still getting closer (not "arrived").
              Removed: the two planted questions, 「三個月內…每月超過 15 萬次閱讀」, 「能。…我以前就做過。」, 「各產業裡最早把 AI 用起來的一批人」,
              「對了一次官方的尺／量的是整套原廠知識體系」, and the closing line borrowed from the home page.
              PARTNER STATUS — DO NOT ADD YET: he wants 「（Anthropic 的台灣認證合作夥伴）」 after 匯流顧問. Certified approval had not arrived on 10/9
              (he wrote to ask on 10/8). Add it only once approved, and in the wording the approval allows.
              Previous version: session scratchpad, about-sky.before-sharing-rewrite.astro. */}
          {/* 10/9 later: the purpose of this last part was settled with the author — it closes the story (why he writes; the life he has now).
              It is not where the offers are listed: the side column and the ending already carry them, and listing them here kept reading as sales copy.
              So: the course is two characters (開課) with no link, companies are told once, the certificate is left to the side column,
              Jira / Polarion moved up as the fourth "before / now" example, and the closing three sentences stand alone.
              The fourth example's second half (「現在帶團隊把 AI 接進流程，用的是同一份經驗」) is Claude's wording; the author agreed to it on 10/9.
              Ending, the author's word (10/9): first "方向對了、還在靠近", then "我覺得已經是過理想的生活了" — so the story ends on having arrived.
              「現在有答案了」 echoes his article minerva-mda-growth. The home page still says 「更靠近自己想過的生活」, on purpose.
              PARTNER STATUS still not to be added after 匯流顧問 until Certified is approved (see the note above).
              Previous version: session scratchpad, about-sky.before-ending-purpose.astro. */}
          <p>研究 AI 和生產力，本來就是我有興趣的事。走過的路、踩過的坑，我很樂意講出去，就寫成文章發在 Facebook 和 Blog。</p>
          <p>我先做的是自己的產品，但寫出去之後，大家來問的是另一件事：我的 AI 工作環境長什麼樣、流程怎麼排、我是怎麼用 AI 的。我就接著寫這些。</p>
          <p>後來有人想跟著做，有公司想導入，我開始<a href="/zh-TW/workshop/" data-umami-event="about_click_workshop_story">開課</a>、進企業帶團隊，也和幾位夥伴成立了<a href="https://confluence-partners.ai/?utm_source=yu-wenhao.com&utm_medium=about" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-umami-event="about_click_confluence">匯流顧問</a>。這些事自然成了我的收入。</p>
          <p>做自己喜歡的事，時間自由，也能幫助別人，這就是我想過的生活。2020 年日記第一天的那個問題，現在有答案了。</p>
        </div>
      </div>

